# Round qtglm2 (card for the dump sitting): ik's CPU node dumps on the glmmixk and glmmix4 fixture variants
# (/models/fixture-variants/<tag>/, GLM's fixture with the mixers retyped: glmmixk q5_K/q6_K/q6_K q, k, v with q5_K
# attn_output and attn_q_a; glmmix4 q4_K q, k, v with q6_K attn_output, attn_q_a and attn_kv_a_mqa and q4_K attn_q_b:
# tools/fixture-variants.tsv), so gate_glm5next_e2e's FixtureOracle clauses on each variant have their sets. The two are
# glmattnk and glmattn4 made again under new tags: the GEMM front's plan reserve counts the K-quant mixer forms
# (place::MixerForms), so the budget the variants record is the planner's value for the new reserve, and a set is keyed by the
# model file's path, so a remade file never sits under the old tag's sets.
# The precedent is glmattn-dump.card (the three variants' nine dumps). Six dumps, each `BLOOMERY_TIER=fixture
# BLOOMERY_FIXTURE_VARIANT=<tag> just dump-ref-fixture glm5next [step4 | step4-every-node]` (the bare form is the batch set)
# under this card, one lease each. Nothing is timed. The dumpers are main's shared bin/ (the ik build the real and fixture sets
# were dumped with); a variant changes the file, not the dumper.
# Minutes [derived from glmattn-dump.card and fxoracle-dump.card's measured terms]: fixed 3-15 s a lease take x 6 = 0.3-1.5 min;
# GLM batch, step4 and step4-every-node ~0.1 min each (fxprobe's GLM batch 4.3 s, CPU, -t 32) x 2 variants = 0.6 min; so
# 0.9-2.1 min, rounded up to 2..8 for a cold read of two 7.8 GB variants (7.8 GB at 1-2 GB/s is 4-8 s each, read once and then warm).
# The two requants (`just fixture-requant glm5next <tag>`) take no lease: llama-quantize on 24 threads under the box guard.
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads (CUDA hidden, no card); beside a timed run or a gate batch it would take their
  cores and memory bandwidth, and the profile takes the lease for every dump; why now: the GLM K-quant mixer variants were
  made again for the GEMM front's plan reserve (round qtglm2) and have no oracle sets, so their FixtureOracle clauses and the
  site mutants cannot run
minutes: 2..8
